  "answer": "This is a new manufacturer field, so I\u2019ll follow the feature playbook and start by reading its steps and the domain model.The website belongs on the manufacturer itself, so every REST view inherits it. Invalid values get rejected at the private create and update boundary before anything is saved.Manufacturers now have an optional `website` URL. It is stored on the manufacturer record, accepted on private create and update, and returned as `website` on manufacturer detail, manufacturer lists, and the manufacturer nested in a product. A non-blank value that does not start with `http://` or `https://` is rejected with HTTP 400 before anything is saved. That follows Model the Domain (one field on the manufacturer), Boundary Discipline (the check sits on the private API, outside the existing error catch), and the Laziness Protocol (no new type).\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 on a bad website\", \"persistence of a valid website\", \"JSON field on manufacturer detail, list, and product\"], \"missing\": [\"a focused manufacturer API test or fixture that posts a website and reads it back\"]}",
